From 43705bf3d619091e842ecdd5c92ee689dd630133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:47:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] R1: the bank plane is a RUNTIME INDEX TENSOR, so the copies
 go AND graph reuse stays

lane-175 closed C4 on the finding that position-derived plane offsets cannot be baked into a
cached graph (F-146). That is true of a baked VIEW OFFSET. It is not true of the plane itself:
llama-kv-cache.cpp:1665 already scatters into a persistent cache at a destination row that
advances every token - ggml_set_rows(k, k_cur, k_idxs) - llama-graph.cpp:519 refills that index
every ubatch, and llama-graph.cpp:544's can_reuse compares only its SHAPE. Runtime-indexed
scatter and graph reuse already coexist in this tree. llama-context.cpp:1732 is why: set_inputs
runs OUTSIDE the can_reuse/build branch, so input tensors are refilled on the reuse path too.

So the ssm bank write becomes ggml_set_rows(ssm_states_2d, snapshots, s_wrow), the K-1 age-shift
copies per layer per ubatch are deleted (lane-168's 2.097 MB/layer/token x 31 layers), and NO
graph offset depends on token position - which is why rs_pos is deliberately absent from
can_reuse here. Adding it back would re-forfeit reuse and reproduce C4's TIE.

Carried from lane-175 verbatim, adding no new cell-layer risk: the corrected two-field
pos_bank/pos_bank_prev anchor and its whole lifecycle (clear sites, seq_cp, the find_slot
gather-and-reorder swap, state_read_meta). ring_anchor_sim.py still gates it.

Two scope cuts, both deliberate:
- The conv bank is NOT rotated. Its F-136 root fix already lands all K planes in one contiguous
  write, so it has no per-plane shift copies to delete. Rotating it buys nothing and costs an
  indirection. The two banks therefore need separate read indices, which is why s_copy2()
  returns both rows in ONE traversal - s_copy() consumes rs_idx, so two passes would resolve
  every rolled-back read to slot 0.
- The rotated read is requested by an explicit /*bank=*/true at exactly the five build_rs call
  sites whose model also calls build_recurrent_attn. mamba, rwkv6/7, plamo2, lfm2, kimi-* and
  minimax cannot pick up a rotation they do not write. No arch enum to drift.

n_seq_max == 1; LLAMA_RS_R1_OFF=1 restores the shipped path in the SAME binary (F-145);
every 2026-08-24 ring diagnostic env var forces the shipped path rather than a hybrid.

F-146 compliance: the only baked offset that still varies is rs_z_bank, and it is added to all
four can_reuse sites in THIS commit. get_rs_pos() still returns a constant when R1 is off.

Gate: r1_index_sim.py - 32480 reads, 0 divergent, both negative controls RED.
